%% Lab 13: agentic RAG. The model requests a search and writes the query; our code runs retrieve and feeds the files
%% back; the model decides whether all facts are found. A missing fact sends it round again with a new query, while
%% our turn cap allows. Exits: an answer, "not in the files", or the cap.
%% Export: npx -y @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i lab13_agentic_rag.mmd -o lab13_agentic_rag.png -b white -s 2
flowchart LR
    q[question<br/>from the rep] --> ask[model requests search<br/>writes the query]
    ask --> run[retrieve runs<br/>embed the query<br/>2 nearest files]
    run --> fed[files fed back<br/>name and text<br/>one tool message]
    fed --> facts{model:<br/>all facts found?}
    facts -->|missing a fact| left{turns<br/>left?}
    left -->|yes: a new query<br/>from what it read| ask
    left -->|no| cap[stopped by the cap<br/>no answer]
    facts -->|yes| answer[final answer<br/>from the files]
    facts -->|not in the files| none[say<br/>I do not know]
    classDef model fill:#0B1220,color:#FFFFFF,stroke:#0B1220
    classDef code fill:#C9F24D,color:#0B1220,stroke:#0B1220
    class ask,facts model
    class run,fed,left code
